  "explain": "This is the **merge step of merge sort** done with pointers. Use a dummy head node and a `tail` pointer. While both lists have nodes, append the node with the smaller value and advance that list. When one list runs out, attach the whole remainder of the other. Each node is visited once: O(n + m) time, and since nodes are relinked rather than copied, O(1) extra space.",
