  "solution": {
   "c": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int n, a[1000];\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) scanf(\"%d\", &a[i]);\n    int low = 0, mid = 0, high = n - 1;\n    while (mid <= high) {\n        if (a[mid] == 0) { int t = a[low]; a[low] = a[mid]; a[mid] = t; low++; mid++; }\n        else if (a[mid] == 1) mid++;\n        else { int t = a[mid]; a[mid] = a[high]; a[high] = t; high--; }\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) printf(i ? \" %d\" : \"%d\", a[i]);\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n    return 0;\n}\n",
   "cpp": "#include <iostream>\n#include <utility>\n#include <vector>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<int> a(n);\n    for (int &x : a) cin >> x;\n    int low = 0, mid = 0, high = n - 1;\n    while (mid <= high) {\n        if (a[mid] == 0) swap(a[low++], a[mid++]);\n        else if (a[mid] == 1) mid++;\n        else swap(a[mid], a[high--]);\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cout << (i ? \" \" : \"\") << a[i];\n    cout << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n",
   "java": "import java.util.*;\n\nclass Main {\n    static void swap(int[] a, int i, int j) { int t = a[i]; a[i] = a[j]; a[j] = t; }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner in = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = in.nextInt();\n        int[] a = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) a[i] = in.nextInt();\n        int low = 0, mid = 0, high = n - 1;\n        while (mid <= high) {\n            if (a[mid] == 0) swap(a, low++, mid++);\n            else if (a[mid] == 1) mid++;\n            else swap(a, mid, high--);\n        }\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) sb.append(i > 0 ? \" \" : \"\").append(a[i]);\n        System.out.println(sb);\n    }\n}\n",
   "py": "import sys\n\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nn = int(data[0])\na = list(map(int, data[1:1 + n]))\nlow = mid = 0\nhigh = n - 1\nwhile mid <= high:\n    if a[mid] == 0:\n        a[low], a[mid] = a[mid], a[low]\n        low += 1\n        mid += 1\n    elif a[mid] == 1:\n        mid += 1\n    else:\n        a[mid], a[high] = a[high], a[mid]\n        high -= 1\nprint(*a)\n"
  },
  "explain": "Dijkstra's **Dutch national flag** algorithm keeps three regions with three pointers: everything before `low` is 0, everything from `high + 1` on is 2, and `mid` scans the unknown middle. If a[mid] is 0, swap it with a[low] and advance both; if it is 1, just advance mid; if it is 2, swap it with a[high] and shrink high (do not advance mid, because the swapped-in value is not checked yet). Each element is examined at most twice: one pass, O(n).",
