  "explain": "The recursive version is three lines: traverse the left child, record the node, traverse the right child. To avoid recursion, simulate it with a **stack**: go as far left as possible pushing nodes; when you cannot go further, pop a node, visit it, and then move to its right child and repeat. Both visit each node once: O(n) time, and O(h) space where h is the height of the tree.",
